  {
   "n": 8,
   "type": "MSQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • COMPUTER SCIENCE & IT • +1 / -0",
   "html": "<p>Which of the following statements are true for every language <em>L</em> ⊆ {0, 1}*?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p><em>L</em>* is infinite.</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<p><em>L</em> is accepted by some DFA if and only if <em>L</em> is accepted by some NFA.</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>If <em>L</em> is the union of two undecidable languages, then <em>L</em> is undecidable.</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "<p>If <em>L</em> is the union of two decidable languages, then <em>L</em> is decidable.</p>"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
